#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:255
msgid "The types are in force over DAYS, not only registered in a month. A calculation register on this chart may keep action periods only when this is on (it refuses to save otherwise), and only then does the Displacing section cut anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:256
msgid "Base dependence"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:256
msgid "Which period of a base record puts it into a base (GetBase). By action period: the days the base record is in force that fall inside the base period, prorated. By registration period: a base record counts whole when it is registered inside the base period. No base (the default): the types take no base."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:257
msgid "Base charts of calculation types"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:257
msgid "The other charts whose types this chart's Base and Leading sections may name - a tax chart whose base is the accruals of another chart, say. This chart's own types may always be named."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:263
msgid "Displacing calculation types"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:263
msgid "For each type, the types that displace it: a record of a named type cuts the days it overlaps out of this type's record for the same dimension values (a sick leave out of a salary). Read as it stands - a change applies at once to records already written."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:265
msgid "Base calculation types"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:265
msgid "For each type, the types whose results make up its base: GetBase sums the records of the named types over the base period, the way the base dependence says (a vacation paid from the salary and bonuses before it)."
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:267
msgid "Leading calculation types"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/backend/metaCollection/partial/chartOfCalculationTypes.h:267
msgid "For each type, the types whose change makes its records stale: a record of a named type written for the same dimension values and meeting in time marks this type's records for recalculation (in a register that keeps recalculation)."
msgstr ""

